<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 7 October, from 3761 BCE to 2001.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">3761 BCE <span class="tih-ago">5,786 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The epoch of the Hebrew calendar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> calendar counts its years from a date equivalent to 7 October 3761 BCE, the traditional date of creation calculated from biblical chronology. Year 1 of this reckoning is still used to number the Jewish year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1513">1513 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">513 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spanish and imperial troops defeat a Venetian army at La Motta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Schio in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veneto">Veneto</a>, a combined Spanish and imperial army under Ramón de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardona">Cardona</a> and Fernando d'Ávalos decisively defeated a Venetian army under Bartolomeo d'Alviano, in a significant battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1571">1571 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">455 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Holy League defeats the Ottoman fleet at Lepanto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">Galleys</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1571">Holy League</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-austria">Don John of Austria</a> destroyed most of the Ottoman fleet off western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Lepanto was the last great battle of oared galleys and ended the image of Ottoman naval invincibility.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1737">1737 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">289 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A cyclone and storm surge devastate Calcutta and Bengal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A violent cyclone struck the Hooghly delta, wrecking ships and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a>. Contemporary reports put the dead at 300,000, a figure modern historians consider greatly exaggerated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1763">1763 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">263 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George III bars settlement west of the Appalachians</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s North American territories, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> issued a proclamation reserving the lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appalachian-mountains">Appalachians</a> for Indigenous nations and forbidding settlement there. The restriction angered colonists.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-proclamation-of-1763">Royal Proclamation of 1763</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American forces defeat Burgoyne in the second Battle of Saratoga</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Saratoga, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, American forces under Horatio Gates and Benedict Arnold decisively defeated General John Burgoyne's British army, which surrendered on 17 October. Burgoyne's surrender persuaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to ally with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, a turning point of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battles-of-saratoga">Battles of Saratoga</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luna 3 photographs the far side of the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet probe Luna 3 took the first photographs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>'s far side, which is never visible from Earth. The grainy images revealed a surface with far fewer dark lunar 'seas' than the near side.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afghanistan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2001">2001 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">25 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US and Britain begin air strikes on Afghanistan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American and British forces began bombing Taliban and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda">al-Qaeda</a> targets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, four weeks after the 11 September attacks. The war toppled the Taliban but lasted nearly twenty years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
